## Concrete improvement suggestions

1. Change canonical `internal-id` from string to `BIGINT UNSIGNED`.
2. Remove `env-state`, `sub-system-id`, and `business-type-id` from the ID itself; store them as columns or infer from table/domain context.
3. Keep `virtual-route-bucket-number` outside the ID as a dedicated routing column.
4. Add explicit `created_at` and never rely on ID order as event order.
5. Define generator operational rules: worker allocation, clock rollback handling, restart policy, and sequence overflow policy.
6. Add a small `generator_version` field or reserve bits so the generator format can evolve without redefining business ID semantics.
7. Use a separate public reference ID for external exposure instead of direct base62 of the internal numeric ID.
8. Provide an official ID decode utility and admin lookup tool rather than embedding more human metadata in the ID.
9. Add coding rules: no routing/business branching by parsing ID prefixes.
10. Capacity-plan sequence bits against worst-case peak per-node QPS, not average QPS.

